 to Interferon alpha is associated with improved outcome in HCV-related cirrhosis: a retrospective study</article-title></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b36-cin-6-0381"><label>36</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mahmood</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Niiyama</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Effect of vitamin E on serum amino transferase and thioredoxin levels in patients with viral hepatitis C</article-title><source>Free Radic. Res</source><volume>37</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>781</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12911275</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-cin-6-0381" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Change in annual average ALT during the follow-up period in HCC patients.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="cin-6-0381f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-cin-6-0381" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>ALT pattern in the non-HCC group throughout the follow-up period.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="cin-6-0381f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-cin-6-0381" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Patient Characteristics at baseline.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">n = 55</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age in years</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">60.8 &#x000b1; 8.2</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sex (M/F)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">(24/31)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">H/O B.T (+)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">43.60%</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">H/O L.D (+)</td><td align="center" rowspan